   "source": [
    "The kaggle dataset, downloaded on 13/02/2026, contains 2 files, a weather parquet file and a cities csv file. The weather file consists of names of cities, date, seasons, and temperature, offering relevant information for our analysis, while the cities file contains countries. Both files have a common column, 'station_id' , that maps each station to a city/country, which can be used to merge the 2 files together for easier analysis. It also has additional data such as precipitation, snow depth, wind direction and speed, sea level pressure and total sunshine. All these data will provide us the necessary information we need to carry out our analysis, when combined with our other datasets covering the gas emissions. The city and country data are especially useful since it is at an appropriate level of granularity to be combined with gases emission data for our analysis. The following code imports the data into a DataFrame and displays the first few rows, thereby giving an idea of the stored data."
   ]
