  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Missing data shown here pretty similar to the country-level data, with CH4 and N2O having the most missing data. We can see that most fuels having many missing records, with 7 fuels having more than 50% missing data. This is likely because most uses of fuels were not regularly reported, leading to gaps in the data. Since it's hard to know that `0` emissions are true zeros or just missing data, we probably not use this dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 45,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1500x1200 with 12 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "gases = [c for c in ds3.columns if c not in (\"country\", \"fuel\", \"year\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "# melt\n",
    "long = ds3.melt(\n",
    "    id_vars=[\"country\", \"fuel\", \"year\"],\n",
    "    value_vars=gases,\n",
    "    var_name=\"gas\",\n",
    "    value_name=\"emission\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# treat 0 as missing\n",
    "long[\"emission\"] = long[\"emission\"].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "# aggregate across country\n",
    "long = (\n",
    "    long.groupby([\"fuel\", \"year\", \"gas\"], as_index=False)[\"emission\"]\n",
    "    .sum(min_count=1)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# global totals per gas-year\n",
    "global_tot = (\n",
    "    long.groupby([\"gas\", \"year\"], as_index=False)[\"emission\"]\n",
    "    .sum()\n",
    "    .rename(columns={\"emission\": \"emission_total\"})\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# merge\n",
    "long = long.merge(global_tot, on=[\"gas\", \"year\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# keep only valid years\n",
    "long = long[long[\"emission_total\"].notna() & (long[\"emission_total\"] > 0)].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# compute ratio\n",
    "long[\"ratio\"] = (long[\"emission\"] / long[\"emission_total\"]).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# plotting\n",
    "n = len(gases)\n",
    "ncols = 3\n",
    "nrows_plot = math.ceil(n / ncols)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axs = plt.subplots(\n",
    "    nrows_plot, ncols,\n",
    "    figsize=(ncols * 5, nrows_plot * 3),\n",
    "    squeeze=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "axs = axs.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, gas in enumerate(gases):\n",
    "    df_g = long[long[\"gas\"] == gas].copy()\n",
    "    df_g = df_g[df_g[\"emission\"].notna()]\n",
    "\n",
    "    pivot = (\n",
    "        df_g.pivot(index=\"year\", columns=\"fuel\", values=\"ratio\")\n",
    "        .fillna(0)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax = axs[i]\n",
    "    pivot.plot.area(ax=ax, linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_title(gas)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Year\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Fuel share of global emissions\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
    "    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if i == 0:\n",
    "        ax.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=\"small\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        legend = ax.get_legend()\n",
    "        if legend:\n",
    "            legend.remove()\n",
    "\n",
    "for j in range(n, len(axs)):\n",
    "    axs[j].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We see from plots that main fuels contributing to each emissions are different and change over time. For example, coal and oil are the main contributors to CO2 emissions, while industrial processes is the main contributor to CH4 and NO2 emissions. This highlights the importance of considering fuel types when analysing emissions trends and their impact on climate change."
   ]
