   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = ds_country.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Year squared feature for non-linear trends\n",
    "df[\"year_squared\"] = df[\"year\"] ** 2\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total emissions\n",
    "df[\"total_emissions\"] = df[gas_cols].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by country and year for lag features\n",
    "df = df.sort_values([\"country\", \"year\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Lag features for emissions\n",
    "lags = [1, 2, 3]  # Lag of 1, 2, and 3 years\n",
    "for gas in gas_cols:\n",
    "    for lag in lags:\n",
    "        df[f\"{gas}_lag{lag}\"] = df.groupby(\"country\")[gas].shift(lag)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop rows with NaN from lags\n",
    "df = df.dropna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We did some feature engineering to create new features that can help us in our predictive analysis. We also created a lag feature for emissions, which is the emission value of the previous year. This can help us capture the temporal dependencies in the data, as emissions in one year are likely to be influenced by emissions in the previous year. We will consider using this lag feature in our predictive models to improve their performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Train-test split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "years = np.sort(df['year'].unique())\n",
    "split_idx = int(len(years) * 0.8)\n",
    "train_years = years[:split_idx]\n",
    "test_years = years[split_idx:]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_df = df[df['year'].isin(train_years)]\n",
    "test_df = df[df['year'].isin(test_years)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop non-feature columns\n",
    "drop_cols = ['AvgTemp', 'ISO3', 'country', 'Continent']\n",
    "X_train = train_df.drop(columns=drop_cols)\n",
    "y_train = train_df['AvgTemp']\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = test_df.drop(columns=drop_cols)\n",
    "y_test = test_df['AvgTemp']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Since this is a time series dataset, we will use a time-based train-test split. We will use the data from first 80% of the years as our training set, and the data from the remaining 20% of the years as our test set. This allows us to train our models on historical data and evaluate their performance on more recent data."
   ]
